upply. The specification lists no such part, and a pull resistor would be expected to reach a signal pin.\", \"evidence\": [{\"source\": \"netlist\", \"quote\": \"(node (ref \\\"R36\\\") (pin \\\"2\\\") (pintype \\\"passive\\\"))\"}, {\"source\": \"netlist\", \"quote\": \"(node (ref \\\"R36\\\") (pin \\\"1\\\") (pintype \\\"passive\\\"))\"}, {\"source\": \"spice\", \"quote\": \"R36 0 +3V3 10k\"}], \"impact\": \"Continuous quiescent load of about 0.33 mA on the 3.3 V LDO output. It is harmless electrically but indicates a stray or misplaced part.\", \"confidence\": 0.25}, {\"category\": \"open_connection\", \"components\": [\"U1\"], \"pins\": [\"U1.2\"], \"nets\": [\"unconnected-(U1-EN-Pad2)\"], \"observed\": \"The TPS62933 buck regulator's EN pin (pin 2) is marked no-connect and is not tied to any net.\", \"expected\": \"EN should be driven or pulled to a defined level, or the design should rely on a documented internal pull-up. Leaving it floating makes regulator startup depend on an internal default.\", \"evidence\": [{\"source\": \"netlist\", \"quote\": \"(net (code \\\"136\\\") (name \\\"unconnected-(U1-EN-Pad2)\\\") (class \\\"Default\\\") (node (ref \\\"U1\\\") (pin \\\"2\\\") (pinfunction \\\"EN\\\") (pintype \\\"input+no_connect\\\")))\"}], \"impact\": \"Possible start-up uncertainty of the 5 V rail, which would power the ESP32 and the 3.3 V LDO. The real impact depends on the part's internal EN default, which the files do not confirm.\", \"confidence\": 0.15}], \"summary\": \"The netlist is mostly consistent with the specification, but the main pump gate resistor R5 is tied to +3V3 rather than GND, which would leave the pump switch on by default. A stray 10k resistor R36 also bridges +3V3 to GND, and the buck regulator EN pin is left unconnected; these are lower-confidence findings.\"}",
